{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And they did not listen to Moses.</b> To reflect on all this in such a way that they would trust in the salvation of the blessed El and account it to themselves as righteousness, as in the case of Abraham. Therefore וְנָתַתִּי אוֹתָהּ לָכֶם (Exodus 6:8) was not fulfilled in them, but was given to their children." "<b>From shortness of spirit.</b> Because their spirit did not believe El, and they did not set their mind to reflect." "<b>And from hard labor.</b> For were it not for the hard labor, they would have set their mind to the words of Moses, and would have understood from his arguments that it is fitting to trust."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:24:37.056632490Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}